{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"TimedEvent","symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"externalID":"s:6Gnusto10TimedEventV","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimedEvent"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimedEvent"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Time, Light, and Death","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DarknessTimeAndDeath","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/fuse(_:after:autostart:perform:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/daemon(_:autostart:perform:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startFuse(_:after:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/stopFuse(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/fuseRemaining(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/startDaemon(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/stopDaemon(_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/isDaemonActive(_:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Time-Light-and-Death"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"TimedEvent"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/DarknessTimeAndDeath","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Timers tick once per typed command, at the very end of the turn (after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the world’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after"},{"type":"text","text":"\/each-turn rules): fuses first, then daemons, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"group in name order. They tick on refused turns (world time passes) but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not on parse errors, meta commands, or once the game has ended. A timer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"started during a turn ticks at the end of that same turn — so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fuse(after: 1)"},{"text":" started by a rule fires as that very turn ends.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TimedEvent"},"abstract":[{"text":"A named timed event, declared in a game or bundle ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timers"},{"type":"text","text":" block: a fuse"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"(fires once, N turns after it is started) or a daemon (runs at the end of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"every turn while active). The body is registered at bootstrap and never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"serialized; only the schedule — name → turns remaining, or the active","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"flag — lives in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WorldState"},{"text":", so it saves and restores like any other","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state and a restore re-binds it to the declared body by name."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/timedevent"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/stopFuse(_:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/stopFuse(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stopFuse","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIden